// English editorial source. Each route has its own visit plan and practical limits.
const g = (slug, name, intro, route, practical, time, source, imageQuery = name) => ({slug, name, intro, route, practical, time, source, imageQuery});
const h = (slug, name, region, style, intro, stay, source, guides) => ({slug, name, region, style, intro, stay, source, guides:guides.map((x,i)=>({...x, hubSlug:slug, url:`/usa/${slug}/${x.slug}/`, index:i}))});
export const usaHubs = [
 h('new-york','New York City','Northeast','metro','Build New York around neighborhoods and subway lines. Downtown harbor history, Midtown institutions and Brooklyn waterfront walks deserve separate blocks of time; crossing the city repeatedly consumes the hours you hoped to spend inside museums.','Allow four to six days. Choose a subway-connected base and verify the exact airport transfer before booking.','https://www.nyctourism.com/',[
 g('lower-manhattan','Lower Manhattan & the Harbor','Lower Manhattan combines the working Financial District, the 9/11 Memorial and the harbor. These are distinct experiences: leave a quiet interval after the memorial, and decide whether an island visit is important before filling the rest of the day.','Start around Battery Park and orient yourself toward the harbor. Visit the memorial respectfully, then choose either a booked museum or a walk through the older streets. A Statue of Liberty or Ellis Island excursion needs its own ticket and security time; the Staten Island Ferry does not land at either island.','Use the official NPS ferry information to identify the authorized departure and ticket. Do not buy from street sellers assuming every harbor cruise includes island access. Check subway weekend changes and keep an indoor alternative for poor weather.','A full day with an island visit; half a day for the mainland streets.','https://www.nps.gov/stli/planyourvisit/index.htm','Statue Liberty New York harbor'),
 g('midtown-central-park','Midtown & Central Park','Midtown works best as a museum or performance day with outdoor breaks. The size of Central Park is easy to underestimate, and an observation deck, a major collection and an evening show can become a rushed sequence if every slot is fixed.','Begin at the institution you most want to see, then walk a manageable stretch of the park. Choose a specific exit near your next subway line. Leave the theater district for the evening if you have a performance booking, with a meal before the crowd reaches the same restaurants.','Compare observation-deck visibility before paying for a timed view. Museums and theaters have separate bag and admission rules. Park distances, heat and winter daylight matter more than the number of pins you have saved.','One full day; reserve a separate day for another large museum.','https://www.centralparknyc.org/','Central Park New York skyline'),
 g('brooklyn-waterfront','Brooklyn Heights & DUMBO','The Brooklyn waterfront offers a different view of the city and a useful slower day. Brooklyn Heights, the promenade and DUMBO connect on foot, but residential streets and busy photography spots should remain usable for people who live and work here.','Arrive by subway, explore the promenade and descend toward Brooklyn Bridge Park. Walk selected waterfront sections and pause for food away from the busiest crossing. Decide whether to cross the Brooklyn Bridge on foot or return by subway before evening fatigue arrives.','Stay out of vehicle lanes for photographs. Waterfront wind and summer sun can be stronger than in sheltered streets. Ferry services have their own boarding and payment arrangements; confirm the destination rather than boarding for an assumed skyline loop.','Half a day to a relaxed full day.','https://brooklynbridgepark.org/','Brooklyn Bridge Park Manhattan')]),
 h('boston','Boston & Cambridge','Northeast','archive','Boston rewards walking in short historical sections, with Cambridge as a separate river crossing. Museums, university streets and harbor departures offer different kinds of days, and winter weather can make an otherwise compact route tiring.','Allow three days. A base near the MBTA network reduces parking and repeated river crossings.','https://www.meetboston.com/',[
 g('freedom-trail','Freedom Trail & North End','The Freedom Trail links places with different histories, admission arrangements and opening hours. Following the entire line is less useful than choosing sites whose interpretation you can actually absorb, then leaving time for the North End as a living neighborhood.','Begin at Boston Common, choose two or three historical interiors and continue toward the North End. Separate a Charlestown extension from the core walk if you want substantial time at the USS Constitution area. Use public transport to return instead of retracing every block.','The marked route does not guarantee that every building is open or free. Cobblestones, stairs and winter ice need an accessibility check. Respect church services, homes and narrow sidewalks when stopping with a group.','Most of a day with interiors; half a day for a shorter section.','https://www.nps.gov/bost/planyourvisit/index.htm','Boston Massachusetts State House'),
 g('cambridge-harvard','Cambridge & Harvard Square','Cambridge is a university city rather than an unrestricted campus attraction. Public streets, museums and river paths provide a full visit, while residence halls, classrooms and research spaces have their own boundaries.','Arrive at Harvard Square and choose a museum or an officially offered tour. Walk public streets toward a meal, then add a short Charles River section if conditions suit. Treat an MIT visit as another neighborhood stop with transit between, rather than an invitation to enter buildings.','University access and tour calendars vary. Verify the specific museum entrance and booking conditions. Avoid photographing people inside private spaces, and shorten the riverside walk during strong wind, snow or summer heat.','Half a day for Harvard Square; a full day with a second institution.','https://www.harvard.edu/visit/','Harvard Yard Cambridge Massachusetts'),
 g('harbor-islands','Boston Harbor & Islands','Boston Harbor can mean a waterfront walk, an island landing or a cruise without a stop. Decide which experience you want before choosing a ticket, and treat the seasonal island ferry as a real transport connection.','Start at the waterfront departure point with time for boarding. If island service is operating, select one island and plan its walking route around the return boat. Otherwise, make the harborwalk and a waterfront institution the day, without advertising an island excursion that is unavailable.','Confirm the current seasonal schedule, island facilities and last return. Food, water and shelter can be limited on islands. Wind can change the service and feel colder offshore; leave room for cancellation rather than tying the boat to a flight.','A half or full day depending on the landing and ferry timetable.','https://www.nps.gov/boha/planyourvisit/index.htm','Boston Harbor Islands Georges Island')]),
 h('philadelphia','Philadelphia','Northeast','brick','Philadelphia combines the independence sites with strong museum and neighborhood days. Keep Old City, the parkway and food-market visits distinct so the trip includes more than a photograph of the Liberty Bell.','Two or three days work well. Compare SEPTA access with the exact hotel location.','https://www.visitphilly.com/',[
 g('old-city','Old City & Independence Park','Old City brings together constitutional history, preserved streets and contemporary residents. Independence Hall and the Liberty Bell have different entry procedures, so the useful first step is to check the official park plan rather than queue at whichever line looks shortest.','Start with the visitor information and your booked interior, then visit the Liberty Bell if the queue fits. Continue through a limited set of historic streets, leaving room to read the interpretation. Finish at a nearby meal rather than adding a distant museum just to fill the afternoon.','Reservation and security requirements can change. Use the NPS information for the visit date. Private houses remain private even on historic lanes, and summer heat makes water and indoor pauses important.','Half a day to a full day with historical interiors.','https://www.nps.gov/inde/planyourvisit/index.htm','Independence Hall Philadelphia'),
 g('parkway-museums','Museum Parkway & Schuylkill River','The parkway contains major art collections separated by broad roads and substantial walking. Choose one collection as the main event; the river is an outdoor complement rather than a reason to rush through galleries.','Visit your selected museum first, then walk an accessible section toward the Schuylkill if weather allows. Use a bridge or signed crossing suited to the route. The famous museum steps can be a short stop, but the collection deserves its own time and admission decision.','Check museum closure days and exhibition tickets. River paths may be affected by flooding or works, and bike traffic shares some sections. Keep an indoor alternative when the parkway is exposed to summer heat or winter wind.','One day with a museum; two to three hours for an outdoor walk.','https://philamuseum.org/','Philadelphia Museum Art Schuylkill'),
 g('reading-terminal','Reading Terminal & Center City','Reading Terminal Market is a working food market whose vendors have individual hours. It fits best into a Center City day, with a clear meal window and time to explore nearby public streets rather than treating every counter as a compulsory stop.','Arrive before the busiest lunch period, compare open stalls and choose a meal. Continue through Center City toward City Hall and a compact neighborhood walk. If you want another museum, confirm its hours before leaving the market rather than assuming an afternoon slot remains.','Vendor availability, payment methods and seating vary. Ask about ingredients directly when allergies matter. Keep aisles clear, request permission for close-up photographs and avoid promising that any particular stall operates every day.','Two to four hours with the surrounding streets.','https://readingterminalmarket.org/','Reading Terminal Market Philadelphia')]),
 h('washington-dc','Washington, DC','Northeast','civic','Washington is a city of substantial institutions, long open spaces and neighborhoods beyond the National Mall. A museum day, a memorial walk and a Georgetown outing work better as separate plans than as one exhaustive circuit.','Allow three to five days, with a Metro-connected base and limited daily museum commitments.','https://washington.org/',[
 g('national-mall','National Mall & Memorials','The Mall looks compact on a map but its memorials are separated by long walks in exposed conditions. Treat commemorative sites as places for reflection and plan water, shade and a transport exit before walking from end to end.','Choose either the western memorials or the central Mall for one outing. Move slowly between the selected sites and pause at interpretation rather than collecting photographs. Add another section on a different morning or evening, using a known Metro station for the return.','Summer humidity, thunderstorms and winter wind change the experience. Follow closures and ceremonial arrangements. Restrooms and drinking water are not at every stop, and the nearest visible building may not be a public shelter.','Half a day for one section; avoid combining every memorial with a full museum.','https://www.nps.gov/nama/planyourvisit/index.htm','Lincoln Memorial reflecting pool'),
 g('smithsonian','Smithsonian Museums & Capitol Hill','The Smithsonian is a group of institutions with different locations and entry arrangements. Pick a subject and a specific museum before planning the day; a free admission policy does not mean all popular entries are available without a reservation.','Use the morning for one collection. After lunch, choose either a short Mall walk or a separately booked Capitol-area visit. Verify the actual address, especially when a museum operates more than one site, and leave time for security and bag checks.','Check timed-entry requirements directly with each institution. Do not confuse the National Mall Air and Space Museum with the Udvar-Hazy Center near Dulles. A Capitol tour is a separate reservation and should not be squeezed between distant museums.','A full day for one major museum and one modest addition.','https://www.si.edu/visit','Smithsonian Castle Washington DC'),
 g('georgetown','Georgetown & the Potomac','Georgetown offers historic streets, shops and a riverfront setting beyond the monumental core. Hills and the lack of a Metro station in the center make the last part of the journey worth planning, particularly for visitors with limited mobility.','Arrive by a confirmed bus or a manageable walk from transit. Explore a few streets, then descend toward the waterfront for a pause. Add an open section of the canal towpath only if conditions and daylight suit, returning through a known stop.','Check path works and river conditions before extending the walk. Canal scenery is not a guarantee of a continuous accessible route. Keep shopping, restaurant queues and a longer river excursion as optional choices rather than booking them all together.','Half a day, or longer with a meal and a selected towpath section.','https://www.nps.gov/choh/planyourvisit/index.htm','Georgetown Washington waterfront')]),
 h('new-england','New England Coast & Mountains','Northeast','coast','Beyond Boston, New England changes from harbor towns to mountain roads and protected coast. Maine, the White Mountains and Vermont need different overnight bases; fall color is weather-dependent and should not be treated as a fixed-date event.','Allow a week for a limited road circuit. Book overnight stops before adding distant scenic detours.','https://www.discovernewengland.org/',[
 g('portland-maine','Portland, Maine & Casco Bay','Portland pairs a compact working waterfront with island ferries and a regional food scene. The Old Port is not the same outing as a distant lighthouse circuit, and ferry choice determines whether you are visiting an island or simply enjoying the crossing.','Walk the Old Port and choose a waterfront meal. For an island afternoon, match the departure to a specific landing and return. Keep a lighthouse visit on another road segment if it needs a car, instead of assuming every coastal landmark is walkable from downtown.','Check seasonal ferry frequencies and island services. Working wharves can be restricted, and weather offshore may be colder than in town. Restaurant bookings and dietary needs deserve advance attention during busy weekends.','Two days for the city and one bay outing.','https://www.visitportland.com/','Portland Maine harbor'),
 g('acadia','Acadia & Mount Desert Island','Acadia offers rocky shore, carriage roads and mountain viewpoints, but the park and Bar Harbor can be busy in different ways. Choose a walking or scenic-driving priority and check which roads, shuttles and reservations apply to it.','Begin at official visitor information, select one manageable trail or carriage-road section and keep a coastal stop for later. Treat Cadillac Summit Road as a separate access decision. Return before fatigue turns narrow roads and crowded parking into the main experience.','Vehicle reservations, entrance passes and trail conditions are separate checks. Stay back from wave-washed rocks. Fall and winter can reduce facilities, and a clear morning does not guarantee a safe exposed summit later.','Two or three days based on Mount Desert Island.','https://www.nps.gov/acad/planyourvisit/index.htm','Acadia National Park coastline'),
 g('white-mountains-vermont','White Mountains & Vermont Roads','Northern New England is a road journey with slow scenic sections and rapidly changing mountain weather. A valley village, a short trail and a mountain-road viewpoint may fit one day; crossing several states while hiking usually does not.','Choose a base on the side of the mountains you will explore first. Use a short signed trail or visitor facility before committing to a higher route. Continue toward Vermont only as a planned overnight transfer, leaving time for villages and legal viewpoints along the way.','Check road closures, trail conditions and daylight. Autumn traffic can be substantial, and foliage timing varies by elevation and weather. Respect farm entrances and private land when stopping for photographs; roadside shoulders are not automatic parking.','Three to five days for one mountain-and-village circuit.','https://www.fs.usda.gov/r09/whitemountain','White Mountains New Hampshire landscape')]),
 h('chicago','Chicago','Great Lakes','grid','Chicago divides naturally into architecture along the river, major lakefront institutions and neighborhood streets. Wind, winter weather and the scale of the lakefront make a transit plan as valuable as a list of buildings.','Allow three days. Stay near useful CTA service and check late-night return options.','https://www.choosechicago.com/',[
 g('loop-riverwalk','The Loop & Chicago Riverwalk','The Loop and Riverwalk reveal the city through architecture, bridges and the working river. A narrated architecture cruise can add context, while a self-guided walk offers flexibility and an easier indoor alternative when weather changes.','Start near the river and identify your cruise pier if booked. Walk a limited stretch of Riverwalk, then move into the Loop for public art or an interior visit. Leave space to stop and look up without blocking commuters or bridge approaches.','Cruises depart from different piers and operate by weather and season. Riverwalk access can change during events or high water. Do not assume a river boat includes lake access, and bring a layer even on a warm day.','Half a day to a full day with an architecture tour.','https://www.architecture.org/','Chicago Riverwalk skyline'),
 g('museum-lakefront','Museum Campus & Lakefront','The lakefront combines major museums with long open paths. Choose one institution and a short outdoor section; the Field Museum, Shedd Aquarium and Adler Planetarium each deserve more than a quick stop between photographs.','Begin with the booked museum or aquarium. After a meal, walk toward a lake viewpoint if conditions are comfortable. Return by a checked bus, rail connection or pickup rather than extending the path until the nearest station becomes a long walk.','Admission products and special exhibitions differ. The shoreline can be windy, icy or very hot, and waves are not a swimming invitation. Verify access needs and events that alter roads around the campus.','A full day for one institution and the nearby shore.','https://www.fieldmuseum.org/visit','Chicago Museum Campus skyline'),
 g('neighborhoods','Wicker Park, Logan Square & Neighborhood Chicago','Neighborhood Chicago rewards a slower food, music or design day. Wicker Park and Logan Square are connected by transit, but they remain residential places with independent businesses, varied hours and evening rhythms.','Choose one neighborhood as the main stop, visit a few open shops or galleries and make a deliberate meal break. Add the second area only when the return train remains simple. For a music night, identify the venue, age rules and final transport before buying tickets.','Restaurant and performance hours change independently. Use normal city awareness and keep valuables secure in crowded places. Ask before close-up photography and avoid presenting residential alleys or private murals as unrestricted attractions.','Half a day in one neighborhood, or an evening with a booked performance.','https://www.choosechicago.com/neighborhoods/','Wicker Park Chicago street')]),
 h('seattle','Seattle & Puget Sound','Pacific Northwest','harbor','Seattle mixes hills, markets, ferries and mountain weather. The waterfront is a good urban starting point; a Rainier day or an island crossing should have its own forecast and transport plan.','Allow three or four days. Stay near light rail or a useful bus corridor.','https://visitseattle.org/',[
 g('pike-place-waterfront','Pike Place & Seattle Waterfront','Pike Place is a working market above the waterfront, with stairs, ramps and different levels. A good visit gives vendors and residents space, then connects to the shore without treating every tourist queue as essential.','Arrive around the hours of the businesses you want to visit, choose a meal and explore a few market levels. Descend by an accessible route to the waterfront, adding one institution or a short promenade section. Save another neighborhood for a separate outing.','Market businesses do not share one schedule. Confirm lift access if stairs are unsuitable. Rain and hills make footwear important, and a ferry terminal on the waterfront is a transport facility with specific boarding rules.','Half a day, longer with a waterfront museum or aquarium.','https://www.pikeplacemarket.org/','Pike Place Market Seattle'),
 g('bainbridge','Bainbridge Island Ferry Day','Bainbridge offers a short island visit built around the ferry and Winslow. Walking passengers can explore the town without a car, while farther beaches and trails require a realistic island transport plan.','Check the Seattle departure and return service, then cross as a foot passenger if Winslow is your focus. Walk into town, choose a museum, garden or meal and leave time to return to the terminal. Keep distant island stops optional unless a bus or vehicle is confirmed.','Ferry queues and service disruptions affect the day. Vehicle travel is a different commitment from walking aboard. Verify accessibility, weather and the final useful return instead of assuming boats operate at the same frequency all evening.','Most of a day from Seattle.','https://wsdot.wa.gov/travel/washington-state-ferries','Bainbridge Island ferry Seattle'),
 g('mount-rainier','Mount Rainier National Park','Mount Rainier is a separate mountain trip, with long access roads and different conditions at each entrance. A city forecast cannot tell you whether a high trail is suitable, and snow can remain well beyond winter.','Choose the park area and entrance before leaving Seattle. Start at an open visitor facility, select a trail suited to current conditions and keep a lower-elevation alternative. Return with enough daylight for the road rather than adding a second distant park sector.','Check NPS alerts, road openings and the current reservation policy. Weather, wildfire smoke and snow affect access. Stay on marked trails, carry suitable layers and water, and avoid promising a summit view on a fixed day.','A long day for one area; two nights nearby make the visit less rushed.','https://www.nps.gov/mora/planyourvisit/index.htm','Mount Rainier mountain meadow')]),
 h('portland-oregon','Portland & the Columbia Gorge','Pacific Northwest','forest','Portland city culture, the Columbia Gorge and the Oregon Coast are three different days. Rain, road conditions and popular trailhead access determine how far a scenic outing should extend.','Use three or four days with a city base and a separate road day.','https://www.travelportland.com/',[
 g('washington-park','Washington Park & Portland Gardens','Washington Park combines gardens, museums and wooded paths with hills that can surprise visitors arriving on foot. Choose a specific garden or institution first, then use the park transport options to connect it with a short outdoor section.','Arrive by transit where practical, visit your main garden and leave room for a quiet walk. Check the distance and gradient before adding another park attraction. Return to a neighborhood meal rather than driving across the city between several short visits.','Gardens have distinct admission and opening rules. Seasonal shuttle service and accessible routes need checking. Rain can make paths slick, and bloom periods change with weather; photographs from another month are not a promise of current flowers.','Half a day to a full day.','https://explorewashingtonpark.org/','Portland Japanese Garden'),
 g('columbia-gorge','Columbia River Gorge','The Gorge is a landscape of waterfalls, cliffs and a working transport corridor. Popular stops need parking or shuttle planning, and a short viewpoint visit is different from a steep trail or a cross-river road circuit.','Choose one side of the river and a small number of open stops. Begin at the trail or waterfall with the most constrained access, then reassess before adding a second walk. Leave daylight for the return, particularly when roads or trailheads are busy.','Check permits, road works and trail closures with the land manager. Rockfall, wildfire damage and winter ice can close familiar routes. Stay on open paths and avoid stopping in traffic lanes for waterfall photographs.','One full day from Portland for a limited section.','https://www.fs.usda.gov/r06/crgnsa','Columbia River Gorge Multnomah Falls'),
 g('oregon-coast','Cannon Beach & the Oregon Coast','The coast is a separate weather system from Portland. Cannon Beach offers a walkable base and striking sea stacks, while a longer coastal drive needs overnight stops and enough time to enjoy the shoreline.','Walk the beach from a legal access point and use tide information to decide how close to intertidal areas to go. Add one open headland viewpoint or town stop. Return inland early if visiting for the day, rather than extending the drive into darkness.','Sneaker waves, drift logs and cold water are serious hazards. Keep distance from the surf and respect wildlife closures around Haystack Rock. Tide-pool access does not permit collecting or disturbing animals.','A full day from Portland; an overnight stay allows a calmer coastal rhythm.','https://stateparks.oregon.gov/','Cannon Beach Haystack Rock')]),
 h('san-francisco','San Francisco & the Bay','California','editorial','San Francisco combines steep streets, distinct neighborhoods and bay crossings. A waterfront day, Golden Gate landscapes and a neighborhood day are easier to enjoy than repeated drives through the city.','Three or four days. Compare transit and walking gradients before choosing accommodation.','https://www.sftravel.com/',[
 g('waterfront-alcatraz','Embarcadero & Alcatraz','The waterfront connects ferry infrastructure, public promenades and Alcatraz departures. An island ticket needs advance attention; ordinary sightseeing cruises can circle the island without landing.','Begin at your confirmed departure pier if visiting Alcatraz. Allow time for the boat, island paths and historical interpretation before returning to the mainland. Keep the Ferry Building or a short Embarcadero walk as the flexible part of the day.','Use the NPS link to find the authorized ticket provider. Pier numbers matter and are separated by substantial walking. Bay wind, hills and accessibility arrangements should be checked before assuming the island is a casual extension.','Most of a day with Alcatraz; half a day for the waterfront alone.','https://www.nps.gov/alca/planyourvisit/index.htm','Alcatraz island San Francisco'),
 g('golden-gate-presidio','Golden Gate & the Presidio','The Golden Gate is a landscape of viewpoints, trails and changing fog. Choose a specific side of the bridge and a realistic walking distance, with the Presidio providing a substantial park visit even when the bridge is partly hidden.','Start at an open Presidio visitor area, walk to one viewpoint and decide whether a bridge crossing fits wind and energy. Use a confirmed bus connection for the return. Leave Marin headlands for a separate plan if you do not have suitable transport.','Bridge pedestrian and bicycle access rules vary by side and time. Fog can arrive quickly; bring layers and stay on signed paths. Do not stop a vehicle on bridge approaches or assume every coastal trail is step-free.','Half a day to a full day.','https://presidio.gov/','Golden Gate Bridge Presidio'),
 g('mission-neighborhoods','Mission District & Neighborhood Walks','The Mission is a living district shaped by Latino culture, art and independent businesses. Murals need context and respectful viewing, while nearby parks and food stops make a better day than a checklist of photo walls.','Choose a compact walking area, seek out public art with local interpretation and pause for a meal. Add a park if conditions suit. Use transit between neighborhoods rather than assuming the city is flat or that every saved stop belongs on the same walk.','Ask before photographing people and businesses. Keep belongings secure and avoid leaving bags in parked cars. Some murals and courtyards are on private property; a social-media location pin is not permission to enter.','Half a day in one district.','https://www.sftravel.com/neighborhoods','Mission District San Francisco murals')]),
 h('los-angeles','Los Angeles','California','cinema','Los Angeles is a collection of districts connected by real travel time. Downtown, Hollywood and the coast work best as separate days, with a hotel base chosen for the first part of the itinerary.','Allow four or five days. Check Metro routes and road travel times for the actual hour.','https://www.discoverlosangeles.com/',[
 g('downtown-arts','Downtown LA & the Arts District','Downtown brings museums, historic streets and a working arts district into a broad area. Choose a few destinations connected by a sensible walking and transit route, rather than treating the whole district as a continuous pedestrian attraction.','Start with a reserved museum or cultural institution, then visit a nearby public space and meal stop. Move to the Arts District only when the route and time suit. Check the return station or pickup location before an evening event.','Museum reservations and closure days differ. Street conditions vary block by block; use current local guidance and ordinary city awareness. Gallery doors and warehouse courtyards are not all open to casual visitors.','One day with a major collection.','https://www.thebroad.org/visit','Walt Disney Concert Hall Los Angeles'),
 g('hollywood-griffith','Hollywood & Griffith Park','Hollywood street attractions and Griffith Observatory are different experiences linked by a significant climb or transport connection. The observatory offers city context, while a hike requires a separate check of weather, daylight and ability.','Keep the Hollywood street visit brief if it is not your main interest. Travel to Griffith by a confirmed route and allow time for the public grounds or observatory. Choose a short marked trail only when conditions suit, then return before darkness complicates the descent.','Check building hours, parking and shuttle information. Heat, fire restrictions and crowded sunset periods can alter access. The Hollywood Sign is viewed from designated public locations; residential roads and fenced areas are not shortcuts.','A full day with a careful sunset return.','https://griffithobservatory.org/visit/','Griffith Observatory Los Angeles'),
 g('santa-monica-venice','Santa Monica & Venice','The western coast offers a beach-and-neighborhood day with a long shared path. Santa Monica and Venice can be linked on foot or bicycle, but sun, distance and return transport deserve as much attention as the pier.','Arrive near the area you want to explore first, walk a limited shore section and take a meal break inland. Continue to Venice only if the group has enough energy and a clear return plan. Use designated bicycle space and dismount where required.','Beach weather may be cooler than inland LA, while sun exposure remains strong. Follow lifeguard advice and separate swimming from a long walk. Keep valuables secure and check transit or pickup options before the evening rush.','Half a day for one area; a full day for both.','https://www.santamonica.com/','Santa Monica pier beach')]),
 h('san-diego','San Diego','California','sun','San Diego mixes cultural institutions, coastal habitats and harbor history. Balboa Park, La Jolla and the bay each support a full day without driving repeatedly across the county.','Three days cover the main contrasts. Choose a base with the transport you intend to use.','https://www.sandiego.org/',[
 g('balboa-park','Balboa Park','Balboa Park is a large cultural landscape with museums, gardens and separate attractions. Choose one or two interests before buying a pass; the zoo is a substantial visit with its own admission and should not be treated as a quick extra.','Start at your chosen museum or garden, then walk a shaded section of the public grounds. Pause for food and reassess before adding a second interior. Use park maps to understand distances and accessible entrances rather than following the shortest-looking line.','Check individual institution hours and ticket coverage. Heat and long walks can affect families and visitors with mobility needs. Do not assume one pass includes every special exhibition or adjacent attraction.','A full day; reserve another day for the zoo if it is a priority.','https://balboapark.org/','Balboa Park San Diego architecture'),
 g('la-jolla','La Jolla Coast','La Jolla combines coastal walks, coves and protected wildlife habitat. The right route follows current access and marine conditions, with clear boundaries between observing animals, swimming and walking on cliffs.','Begin at a legal coastal access point, use designated paths and observe wildlife from a respectful distance. Choose a short village meal break before another shore section. Book water activities only with an operator who can explain the conditions and cancellation policy.','Seasonal closures and wildlife protections change access. Never approach sea lions or seals for a photograph, and do not assume a calm-looking cove has no currents. Tide, surf and cliff edges matter throughout the visit.','Half a day on land; a separate session for a guided water activity.','https://www.sandiego.gov/lifeguards/beaches','La Jolla Cove coast'),
 g('harbor-coronado','San Diego Harbor & Coronado','The harbor offers maritime museums, public waterfront and a ferry connection to Coronado. Choose between a substantial museum visit and a longer bay outing so the day does not become a sequence of queues and transfers.','Visit the booked maritime attraction first, then take a waterfront break. If crossing to Coronado, identify the landing and the distance to the part of the island you want to see. Return by a confirmed ferry or road option before evening plans.','Ferries, museums and harbor cruises have separate tickets. The Coronado landing is not immediately beside every beach attraction. Check walking distance, bicycle rules and weather, and leave time for boarding rather than reaching the pier at departure time.','One full day for a museum and a limited bay crossing.','https://www.midway.org/visit','San Diego harbor Coronado')]),
 h('sierra-parks','Yosemite & the Sierra Parks','Western Parks','granite','Yosemite, Sequoia and Kings Canyon are separate park visits connected by substantial roads. Elevation, snow, fire and entrance choice determine the itinerary; a national park pass does not replace every reservation.','Allow several nights and choose bases near the correct entrances.','https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/index.htm',[
 g('yosemite-valley','Yosemite Valley','Yosemite Valley offers dramatic views without requiring a difficult hike. The valley floor, waterfalls and higher trails have very different effort and access requirements, so build a first visit around open low-level routes and a realistic parking plan.','Start early at the entrance appropriate to your accommodation. Use official visitor information and available valley transport to choose one walk. Keep time for viewpoints and interpretation, then return before traffic or darkness makes the exit harder.','Check the current entry policy rather than repeating a previous year’s reservation rule. Waterfall flow is seasonal. Stay back from water edges and never enter closed trails; snow, rockfall, smoke and road works can change the plan.','Two days in or near the valley for an unhurried introduction.','https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/index.htm','Yosemite Valley Tunnel View'),
 g('sequoia-giant-forest','Sequoia Giant Forest','The Giant Forest is a high-elevation landscape reached by winding roads. Seeing the giant sequoias can be a short, accessible-focused outing or a longer walk, but the road and weather should be assessed before adding distant park sectors.','Choose the correct entrance, stop at open visitor information and select a signed grove route. Allow time to experience the trees slowly. Use seasonal transport where operating and keep a clear return point before the descent.','Check road restrictions, chain requirements, fire impacts and trail conditions. Large vehicles may face limits on winding roads. Protect roots by staying on paths and do not climb fences or enter closed restoration areas.','A full day from a nearby base; more time for additional trails.','https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/index.htm','Sequoia National Park Giant Forest'),
 g('kings-canyon','Kings Canyon & Grant Grove','Grant Grove and the deeper canyon are not interchangeable stops. Seasonal road access can make the canyon unavailable while the grove remains a worthwhile destination, so choose the actual park area before committing to a drive.','Begin with a grove walk and current ranger information. Continue down the canyon road only if it is open and the day allows the full return. Select one valley or river viewpoint and keep distance from fast water.','Road closures and limited fuel or food services require advance planning. A summer photograph does not establish current conditions. Check the final open road segment and avoid adding a long hike after a tiring mountain drive.','One day for Grant Grove; another day for an open canyon-road excursion.','https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/conditions.htm','Kings Canyon National Park canyon')]),
 h('las-vegas','Las Vegas & Southern Nevada','Southwest','neon','Las Vegas has large indoor venues and long outdoor distances. The Strip, downtown and desert parks need different plans; air-conditioned interiors do not remove the heat risk between them.','Two or three city days, with a separate desert outing if conditions suit.','https://www.visitlasvegas.com/',[
 g('strip','The Strip & Shows','The Strip is longer and slower to walk than its map suggests. Hotels have large interiors, indirect crossings and separate entrances for performances, so a good evening is built around one booked event and a limited area.','Choose the show or restaurant first, then group nearby stops around it. Confirm the venue entrance and arrival time. Use an appropriate transit or pickup option for distant hotels instead of trying to walk the entire corridor between reservations.','Compare total accommodation charges and ticket conditions before paying. Outdoor heat, crowds and late-night fatigue matter. Gambling is optional; set a spending limit if participating and never treat it as a way to fund the trip.','An afternoon and evening in one part of the Strip.','https://www.visitlasvegas.com/','Las Vegas Strip night'),
 g('downtown','Downtown Las Vegas','Downtown has a different scale from the Strip, with historic casino streets, museums and evening entertainment. A cultural stop can explain the city beyond neon, while the busiest pedestrian sections become loud and crowded after dark.','Book a museum or guided interpretation first, then explore a compact downtown area. Take a meal break before evening crowds build and identify your return transport. Avoid adding a distant Strip show unless the transfer has a generous margin.','Some venues and events have age restrictions. Verify opening hours, bag policies and the actual neighborhood route. Use normal city awareness and keep valuables secure when moving through dense entertainment crowds.','Half a day and an evening.','https://www.neonmuseum.org/','Fremont Street Las Vegas'),
 g('red-rock','Red Rock Canyon','Red Rock Canyon is a desert visit with seasonal access rules and a real heat budget. Scenic driving and a short marked walk can make a full outing without attempting a strenuous trail.','Check the official scenic-drive reservation information, begin at the visitor center and choose one trail matched to conditions. Carry water before entering. Leave time for the return to the city and keep a no-hike alternative in extreme heat.','Entry arrangements, closures and weather warnings change. Flash flooding can affect washes, and shade is limited. Stay on established routes, leave rock art and habitat undisturbed, and do not rely on mobile reception for navigation.','Half a day in suitable weather.','https://www.blm.gov/programs/national-conservation-lands/nevada/red-rock-canyon','Red Rock Canyon Nevada')]),
 h('utah-parks','Utah Canyon Country','Southwest','strata','Utah’s parks are separate landscapes with long transfers between them. Zion, Bryce and the Moab area reward different bases, and a short trip should choose fewer parks rather than spend every daylight hour driving.','Allow a week for a selected circuit, with nights near the parks you enter.','https://www.visitutah.com/',[
 g('zion','Zion Canyon','Zion’s main canyon uses transport and trail rules that depend on season and route. A riverside introduction is different from a permit-controlled hike, and neither should be chosen solely because an online itinerary calls it essential.','Check the current shuttle and parking arrangements, then begin with visitor information and an open trail suited to the group. Keep time for viewpoints and the return shuttle. Treat a demanding or water-based route as a separate decision with appropriate preparation.','Check permits, flash-flood forecasts, heat and river advisories directly with NPS. Narrow canyon routes can be unsafe even when rain is elsewhere. Turn back when conditions or ability do not support the plan.','Two days near Springdale for a flexible first visit.','https://www.nps.gov/zion/planyourvisit/index.htm','Zion National Park canyon'),
 g('bryce','Bryce Canyon','Bryce’s high rim can be cold and windy while descents require a climb back out. Viewpoints provide a complete introduction, and a short trail should be selected according to current ice, heat and personal ability.','Start with a rim viewpoint and visitor information. Choose a short open loop only after checking elevation and the return climb. Leave room for another viewpoint or a ranger program instead of driving every spur road.','Altitude, lightning and winter ice affect access. Stay away from unstable edges and follow trail closures. A sunrise visit needs warm layers and a safe drive in darkness; do not assume desert destinations are always hot.','One or two days with a nearby overnight.','https://www.nps.gov/brca/planyourvisit/index.htm','Bryce Canyon hoodoos'),
 g('moab-arches-canyonlands','Moab, Arches & Canyonlands','Moab serves two major parks with separate entrances and different distances. Arches viewpoints and Canyonlands’ Island in the Sky can each fill a day, while remote sectors require another level of preparation.','Choose one park per day, verify the current entrance arrangement and start with a manageable walk. Return to town for supplies before another park day. Keep remote roads and longer backcountry routes outside a casual rental-car itinerary.','Check entry reservations, road suitability, heat and flash-flood warnings. Carry water and protect biological soil crust by staying on trails. A vehicle capable of reaching a paved viewpoint is not automatically suitable for unpaved park roads.','Three nights in Moab for two park days and some flexibility.','https://www.nps.gov/arch/planyourvisit/index.htm','Arches National Park Delicate Arch')]),
 h('arizona','Arizona & the Grand Canyon','Southwest','desert','Arizona combines major elevation changes, desert cities and sovereign Tribal lands. Grand Canyon views, Sedona trails and Phoenix culture belong to separate days with season-specific driving and walking plans.','Allow five or more days for a limited circuit. Check heat and entrance distances before booking bases.','https://www.visitarizona.com/',[
 g('grand-canyon','Grand Canyon South Rim','The South Rim supports a meaningful visit from viewpoints and rim paths alone. Descending below the rim adds heat, distance and a demanding return climb; it should not be treated as a casual extension of a viewpoint stop.','Begin with current visitor information, use available park transport and choose a short rim section. Stay for changing light if you have nearby accommodation. Plan a below-rim hike separately, with current NPS guidance and a conservative turnaround.','South and North Rim access are separate journeys. Check fire impacts, road openings, water availability and current alerts. Keep away from unprotected edges and never feed wildlife, even in busy visitor areas.','Two days or one full day with a nearby overnight.','https://www.nps.gov/grca/planyourvisit/index.htm','Grand Canyon South Rim'),
 g('sedona','Sedona & Red Rock Trails','Sedona combines a town visit with red-rock trails whose parking and heat conditions need planning. Choose a route for its grade and access rather than following a social-media location that may be crowded or restricted.','Use current trailhead and shuttle information, walk one suitable trail early and leave a meal or gallery visit for later. Add another short stop only if daylight and energy remain. Keep the return road simple after a demanding walk.','Trailhead passes and parking rules differ. Carry water, respect closures and avoid stepping off trails onto fragile ground. Cultural places and private property require specific permission; scenic surroundings do not make every path public.','Two days for one substantial walk and town time.','https://visitsedona.com/','Sedona red rocks landscape'),
 g('phoenix-scottsdale','Phoenix & Scottsdale','The Phoenix area is a broad desert metropolis with museums, gardens and severe seasonal heat. A cultural day can be rewarding without a summit hike, especially when temperatures make exposed trails inappropriate.','Choose a museum or garden as the main visit, then group a meal and nearby neighborhood stop around it. If walking outdoors, use the coolest suitable part of the day and a short route. Leave long cross-city transfers outside tight reservations.','Check heat warnings, trail closures and opening hours. Bring water and sun protection, and avoid leaving people or animals in parked cars. Gardens and desert preserves have distinct admission, transport and accessibility arrangements.','Two days with a heat-aware plan.','https://www.visitphoenix.com/','Desert Botanical Garden Phoenix')]),
 h('colorado','Denver & the Colorado Rockies','Mountain West','alpine','Denver provides a city base, while mountain parks and ski towns operate by elevation and season. Build in time to adjust and avoid treating a high-altitude drive as an easy city excursion.','Allow four to six days for Denver and one mountain area.','https://www.colorado.com/',[
 g('denver','Denver Union Station & Museums','Denver’s central neighborhoods work well as an arrival day with a museum, food and a modest walk. The airport rail connection can simplify arrival, but mountain travel is a separate transport commitment.','Begin around Union Station, choose a cultural institution and explore one nearby neighborhood. Use the day to organize any later rental car or mountain transfer. Keep strenuous activity limited if you have just arrived and are unsure how altitude affects you.','Check rail service, museum hours and event crowds. Hydration and a slower pace can help comfort, but symptoms should not be ignored. A Denver hotel does not make a distant trailhead a short morning trip.','One or two city days before a mountain stay.','https://www.denver.org/','Denver Union Station'),
 g('rocky-mountain','Rocky Mountain National Park','Rocky Mountain National Park has distinct entrance and corridor arrangements. Bear Lake access, a scenic road and a long hike are different plans, and timed-entry products may cover different areas.','Choose the corridor first, check the relevant reservation and start at an open visitor facility. Walk a suitable trail and retain a lower-elevation alternative. Keep the return before afternoon weather or fatigue makes exposed terrain less forgiving.','Confirm timed entry, road openings, snow and lightning guidance with NPS. A park pass alone may not reserve entry. Altitude can affect visitors differently; stop and seek appropriate help if symptoms worsen rather than pushing toward a summit.','Two days near a suitable park entrance.','https://www.nps.gov/romo/planyourvisit/index.htm','Rocky Mountain National Park Bear Lake'),
 g('mountain-towns','Colorado Mountain Towns','Colorado’s mountain towns offer trails, historic streets and winter sports, but a resort name does not describe current road or lift conditions. Choose one valley or town as a base and let the season determine the activities.','Arrive in daylight, settle into the town and check local information before taking a high route. Select one lift, trail or cultural visit for the next day. Keep a spare day for weather instead of changing hotels every night.','Snow, chain or traction rules, wildfire smoke and thunderstorms can affect roads. Rental equipment and lessons have separate terms. Do not assume a scenic summer drive is open in winter or that an open lift makes every trail suitable.','Three nights in one mountain area.','https://www.cotrip.org/','Breckenridge Colorado mountains')]),
 h('yellowstone-tetons','Yellowstone & Grand Teton','Mountain West','wildlife','Yellowstone and Grand Teton combine long park roads with geothermal landscapes and wildlife. Entrance selection and overnight bases matter; a single day cannot do justice to both parks.','Allow five to seven days with nights near the areas being visited.','https://www.nps.gov/yell/planyourvisit/index.htm',[
 g('geyser-basins','Yellowstone Geyser Basins','The geyser basins are fragile thermal landscapes, not ordinary walking terrain. Boardwalks provide access to dramatic features, and a predicted eruption should be treated as an estimate rather than a guaranteed appointment.','Choose one basin area for the morning and walk only open boardwalks and paths. Use current ranger information for eruption predictions. Add another nearby feature only if road time and daylight allow, leaving room for slow traffic.','Stay on designated surfaces and keep children close. Thermal water and thin crust can cause severe injury. Check closures and parking conditions, and never enter restricted ground to improve a photograph.','One full day for a limited set of basins.','https://www.nps.gov/yell/planyourvisit/thermal-basin-exploring.htm','Yellowstone Grand Prismatic Spring'),
 g('canyon-lamar','Yellowstone Canyon & Wildlife Valleys','The canyon and northern valleys offer different scenery from the geyser basins. Wildlife viewing is uncertain and should be based on patient observation from legal pullouts, not on approaching animals or chasing sightings.','Choose either a canyon-focused day or a northern valley drive depending on your base. Stop at designated viewpoints and allow time for traffic. Keep a planned return route and avoid adding a distant basin simply because it appears on the same park map.','Follow NPS wildlife distances and carry appropriate equipment for any hike. Never stop in a traffic lane or feed animals. Road openings, snow and animal activity change quickly; dawn viewing requires a safe drive and warm clothing.','A separate full day for each side of the park.','https://www.nps.gov/yell/planyourvisit/photography.htm','Yellowstone Grand Canyon waterfall'),
 g('grand-teton','Grand Teton & Jackson','Grand Teton offers mountain views, lakes and substantial hiking, with Jackson as one possible gateway. A scenic roadside visit can stand alone; a boat crossing or mountain trail adds separate schedules and preparation.','Start at official visitor information and choose one lake or trail area. Use legal viewpoints and leave time to stop quietly. If taking a lake boat, confirm the last return and what happens if the service stops.','Weather and wildfire smoke can hide the range. Keep wildlife distance and follow bear-safety guidance. Parking fills at popular trailheads, and cold water remains dangerous even when the air is warm.','Two or three days in the valley.','https://www.nps.gov/grte/planyourvisit/index.htm','Grand Teton mountains lake')]),
 h('new-orleans','New Orleans','South','jazz','New Orleans deserves time for music, food and the history behind its neighborhoods. The French Quarter, Garden District and river landscape provide different days, with heat and storms shaping the pace.','Three or four days, with a walkable base and a checked evening return.','https://www.neworleans.com/',[
 g('french-quarter','French Quarter & Live Music','The French Quarter is a lived neighborhood as well as a visitor district. Architecture, museums and music can make a rich day without assuming that nightlife is the only reason to visit.','Explore a compact daytime route, choose an interpreted historical stop and pause for food. For evening music, select a venue by the performance and entry rules. Leave time between dinner and the show and identify your way back before the streets become crowded.','Venue hours, age restrictions and cover charges differ. Respect homes and performers, and ask about photography. Heat, rain and large events can change walking routes and transport; keep your belongings secure in crowds.','A day and an evening, with time for a slower return.','https://www.neworleans.com/plan/neighborhoods/french-quarter/','New Orleans French Quarter Jackson Square'),
 g('garden-district','Garden District & Streetcars','The Garden District offers residential architecture and a slower street-level view of the city. Streetcars are useful transport, but service changes and stops should be checked rather than treating them as a guaranteed sightseeing loop.','Ride to a confirmed stop, walk a short public-street route and take a meal or shop break on a nearby commercial street. Return before heat or rain turns the walk into an endurance test. A guided architecture tour can add context without entering private grounds.','Homes, gardens and some cemeteries have access restrictions. Do not step into yards for photographs. Check accessibility and service alerts with the transit operator, especially if a streetcar replacement changes the planned return.','Half a day.','https://www.norta.com/','New Orleans Garden District streetcar'),
 g('river-wetlands','Mississippi River & Wetlands','The riverfront and surrounding wetlands are separate experiences. A city promenade needs little logistics, while a boat excursion outside town depends on a named operator, pickup point, weather and environmental practice.','Choose the riverfront for an urban walk or book one clearly described wetland trip. Confirm whether transport from the city is included. Leave the rest of the day flexible so a delayed pickup or weather cancellation does not collide with another prepaid event.','Ask about wildlife practices and avoid operators that encourage feeding or handling wild animals. Heat, insects and storms affect comfort. A boat trip does not guarantee sightings, and flood conditions can change routes and access.','Half a day on the riverfront or most of a day for an out-of-town excursion.','https://www.nps.gov/jela/planyourvisit/index.htm','Jean Lafitte Barataria wetlands')]),
 h('atlanta','Atlanta','South','culture','Atlanta’s civil-rights history, cultural institutions and neighborhood trails deserve separate attention. Distances and traffic reward grouping visits by district and using MARTA where it serves the plan.','Three days with a base near your main institutions or useful transit.','https://discoveratlanta.com/',[
 g('king-historic-district','Martin Luther King, Jr. Historic District','The historic district is a place of living worship and civic memory. Give its interpretation time and distinguish public visitor areas from active church services and spaces with controlled access.','Begin with NPS visitor information, follow the open historical sites and leave a quiet break afterward. Choose a nearby meal or neighborhood walk rather than moving immediately into unrelated entertainment. Verify the specific building you hope to enter before making it the day’s centerpiece.','Tours, building access and commemorative events can change. Follow photography guidance and respect visitors with personal connections. Do not assume every site named in an older guide is currently open for interior visits.','Half a day with space for reflection.','https://www.nps.gov/malu/planyourvisit/index.htm','Martin Luther King Atlanta historic park'),
 g('midtown-museums','Midtown Museums & Piedmont Park','Midtown combines art institutions, gardens and parkland in a manageable city day. Select one major collection first, then use the park as a flexible outdoor break instead of trying to enter every attraction.','Visit the chosen museum, pause for lunch and continue to an open park section or garden. Check the distance to your return station before adding another stop. A garden ticket and special event may need separate arrangements from museum admission.','Summer heat and thunderstorms can change outdoor plans. Confirm closure days, exhibition tickets and access routes. Keep an indoor option and use signed crossings rather than treating wide roads as informal pedestrian space.','One full day.','https://high.org/visit/','Piedmont Park Atlanta skyline'),
 g('beltline','Atlanta BeltLine & Neighborhoods','The BeltLine links neighborhoods through shared public space, but it is not one uniform route. Choose a completed section with the food, art or park stops you want, and respect bicycle traffic and residential edges.','Start at a known access point, walk a limited section and take an off-path meal break. Continue only if the next connection is open and the return is clear. Public art adds interest, but shops and venues follow their own schedules.','Check construction and trail information before assuming a continuous connection. Keep clear of cyclists and avoid blocking the path for photographs. Hot afternoons require water and shade, and evening return transport should be decided in advance.','Two to four hours for one section.','https://beltline.org/','Atlanta BeltLine trail')]),
 h('texas','Texas Cities','South','road','Texas city visits involve real intercity distances. Austin, San Antonio and Houston each support their own stay; choose a limited combination and account for heat, traffic and the exact location of major attractions.','Allow a week for two cities, with transfer days kept light.','https://www.traveltexas.com/',[
 g('austin','Austin & Lady Bird Lake','Austin combines state-capitol history, music and a central lake trail. A compact daytime route and a separate music evening work better than driving between every restaurant and viewpoint.','Choose a museum or capitol-area visit, then walk a short lake-trail section in suitable weather. Take a break before an evening performance and check venue entry rules. Keep the return transport simple rather than assuming late-night pickups are equally available everywhere.','Heat and storms affect outdoor plans. The lake trail does not make the water an unrestricted swimming area. Confirm attraction hours and respect residential streets when seeking music or food venues beyond the center.','Two or three days.','https://www.austintexas.org/','Austin Texas Lady Bird Lake'),
 g('san-antonio','San Antonio Missions & River Walk','The downtown River Walk and the mission sites provide different historical settings. The missions are active cultural and religious places, and visiting them all requires transport planning beyond a short downtown stroll.','Begin with your main historical site and its current entry arrangement. Take a limited River Walk section and a meal break. Reserve another day or a substantial afternoon for selected missions, choosing transport that matches heat and distance.','Check reservations and opening hours for individual sites. Respect worship and photography rules. Do not assume a riverfront hotel makes the whole mission route walkable, or that cycling is comfortable in extreme heat.','Two days for downtown and a mission-focused outing.','https://www.nps.gov/saan/planyourvisit/index.htm','San Antonio Mission San Jose'),
 g('houston','Houston Museums & Space Center','Houston’s Museum District and Space Center Houston are far enough apart to deserve different days. Decide whether art, science or space history is the priority before choosing accommodation and transport.','Use one day for a selected Museum District institution and a nearby park. Plan the space-center outing separately, confirming the exact ticket, tour options and road transfer. Leave time for traffic and a meal rather than booking another city attraction immediately afterward.','Tour availability and security conditions may differ from general admission. Check what is included and which facilities are actually visited. Heat, heavy rain and flood alerts can disrupt roads; use current local information.','Two or three days, including a separate space-center day.','https://spacecenter.org/visitor-information/','Space Center Houston')]),
 h('miami','Miami & South Florida','Florida','tropical','Miami’s beach, urban art districts and nearby wetlands are distinct visits. Choose a base by the first days of the trip, and keep a car-based Everglades outing separate from a beach evening.','Three or four days with weather flexibility.','https://www.miamiandbeaches.com/',[
 g('south-beach','South Beach & Art Deco','South Beach pairs architectural streets with an exposed Atlantic shoreline. A neighborhood walk can add context to a beach visit, but heat, storms and ocean conditions should determine when and where to swim.','Walk a compact Art Deco route in the cooler part of the day, then take an indoor meal break. Use a lifeguarded beach section only when current flags and advice support it. Keep the evening local rather than scheduling a long cross-city transfer after a full day outside.','Parking and traffic can be difficult during events. Respect residents and hotel boundaries. Follow beach flags, lightning warnings and lifeguards; a busy beach or attractive water color is not proof of safe conditions.','One day at a relaxed pace.','https://www.mdpl.org/','Miami South Beach Art Deco'),
 g('little-havana-wynwood','Little Havana & Wynwood','Little Havana and Wynwood offer different cultural settings and need transport between them. Choose the food, history or art you want to understand, and avoid reducing either neighborhood to a few staged photographs.','Spend a morning in one district with a locally interpreted visit or meal. Move to the second only if heat and travel time allow. Galleries and art attractions may require tickets; public street art can be appreciated without entering private lots.','Ask before photographing people, performers or businesses. Opening hours vary, and walking routes should be checked locally. Keep an indoor pause and secure belongings when using rides or parking between districts.','Half a day in each area.','https://www.miamiandbeaches.com/','Little Havana Miami Calle Ocho'),
 g('everglades','Everglades National Park','The Everglades is a large protected landscape with several gateways. Shark Valley and the southern park entrance are separate outings, so choose an area before buying a tour or planning a drive.','Check the chosen entrance and open facilities, then begin with a ranger-informed boardwalk or guided activity. Keep walking modest in hot conditions and allow time for wildlife observation from a distance. Return before storms or fatigue make the road harder.','Water levels, mosquitoes, heat and seasonal services affect the visit. Keep away from alligators and never feed wildlife. Airboat trips vary in location and operating rules; do not assume every commercial tour enters the national park.','A full day for one gateway.','https://www.nps.gov/ever/planyourvisit/index.htm','Everglades National Park Anhinga Trail')]),
 h('orlando','Orlando & Central Florida','Florida','play','Orlando needs careful separation of resort days, city visits and the Space Coast. Theme-park ticket systems, long walks and summer storms can dominate the trip if there are no rest days.','Allow several days for a limited set of parks, plus recovery time.','https://www.visitorlando.com/',[
 g('theme-parks','Orlando Theme-Park Planning','A theme-park day begins with the exact park and ticket conditions, not a list of every ride. Resorts have different transport systems, and moving between parks can consume substantial time.','Choose one main park, confirm the current admission and reservation requirements and prioritize a few experiences. Plan meals, breaks and the return transport. Keep another park for a different day unless you deliberately purchased and understood a multi-park product.','Ride access, height restrictions and paid queue products change. Check directly with the operator. Heat, thunderstorms and long queues need water, rest and a flexible plan; avoid promising that any attraction is always operating.','One full day per selected park, with rest days between demanding visits.','https://www.visitorlando.com/things-to-do/','Orlando theme park castle'),
 g('winter-park','Winter Park & Orlando Beyond Resorts','Winter Park offers museums, gardens and a walkable commercial center beyond the resort corridors. It is a useful slower day, but the journey from a theme-park hotel still needs a real transport plan.','Choose one museum or garden, walk the central streets and take an unhurried meal. A lake boat outing can be added if the weather and current schedule suit. Return before committing to another distant evening event.','Independent institutions and boat services have their own opening days and tickets. Afternoon storms can interrupt outdoor activities. Check the exact pickup or rail connection rather than assuming every resort shuttle serves Winter Park.','Half a day to a full day.','https://cityofwinterpark.org/','Winter Park Florida Park Avenue'),
 g('kennedy-space-center','Kennedy Space Center & Space Coast','Kennedy Space Center is a separate east-coast outing from Orlando. The visitor complex, optional tours and launch viewing have different availability; a launch should never be promised as part of a routine visit.','Book the visitor product that matches your interests, leave early enough for the road transfer and begin with the most time-sensitive included activity. Keep the whole day for the complex rather than adding a beach circuit and an Orlando dinner deadline.','Check operating hours, tour availability and any event restrictions. Launch schedules can change or be canceled. Confirm whether transport is included in a package and leave extra road time after a major event.','One full day from Orlando.','https://www.kennedyspacecenter.com/','Kennedy Space Center rocket garden')]),
 h('alaska','Alaska Gateways & Parks','Alaska','expedition','Alaska requires choosing a region before choosing activities. Anchorage and the Kenai Peninsula, Denali and Southeast Alaska use different road, rail, boat and flight connections; combining them needs time and weather flexibility.','Allow a week or more for one region. Avoid tightly linked small-aircraft and international departures.','https://www.travelalaska.com/',[
 g('anchorage-kenai','Anchorage, Seward & Kenai Fjords','Anchorage is a practical gateway, while Seward and the fjords deserve a separate overnight. Road or rail travel is part of the experience and should not be compressed around a boat departure with no margin.','Use Anchorage for supplies and cultural context, then transfer to Seward in daylight or on a confirmed train. Choose a named fjord cruise or an open land-based park visit the next day. Keep weather flexibility before returning to Anchorage.','Boat routes, sea conditions and wildlife sightings vary. Check current Exit Glacier access and trail conditions. Pack layers and confirm what food, equipment and transfers the operator includes rather than inferring it from the tour name.','Three to five days for this corridor.','https://www.nps.gov/kefj/planyourvisit/index.htm','Kenai Fjords glacier Alaska'),
 g('denali','Denali National Park','Denali is a large protected landscape with a park road whose accessible length and transport arrangements can change. Plan around current NPS information and a nearby base, not an old photograph of a road endpoint.','Begin at the visitor area, choose an available bus or guided option and reserve another day for an appropriate local trail. Leave time for weather and wildlife observation. Keep the return to your next transport connection comfortably separate from the park outing.','Check road access, bus schedules and trail conditions for the exact season. Wildlife distance and bear-safety guidance apply even near busy facilities. Mountain visibility is uncertain, and a park visit can still be worthwhile without a clear summit view.','Two or three nights near the entrance.','https://www.nps.gov/dena/planyourvisit/index.htm','Denali National Park landscape'),
 g('juneau-southeast','Juneau & Southeast Alaska','Juneau and the Inside Passage operate through flights, ferries and local excursions. They are not road extensions of Anchorage, and a short port call has very different limits from an independent multi-night stay.','Choose the arrival and overnight base first. Use one day for a cultural or town visit and another for a glacier-area or marine excursion with a confirmed operator. Keep time between weather-sensitive travel and onward departures.','Check ferry schedules, flight connections and current glacier-area access. Boat and air excursions can be canceled. Respect wildlife and local communities, and do not assume a cruise-port pickup serves independent travelers from every hotel.','Three or more days in one Southeast gateway.','https://www.traveljuneau.com/','Juneau Alaska Mendenhall Glacier')]),
 h('hawaii','Hawaii','Pacific Islands','island','Hawaii is an archipelago of distinct islands, communities and landscapes. Choose one island for a short stay and allow real transfer time between islands; cultural respect and ocean conditions should shape the itinerary.','A week on one island allows a better pace than daily flights between islands.','https://www.gohawaii.com/',[
 g('oahu','Oahu: Honolulu & Windward Coast','Oahu combines an urban stay with coastal roads and important historical places. Waikiki, Pearl Harbor and the windward coast deserve separate plans, with traffic and timed access accounted for.','Use one day for Honolulu culture and a short beach visit. Reserve a separate historical-site visit if it is a priority, checking the exact ticket and entry procedure. Explore the windward coast on another day with legal stops and a simple return route.','Follow ocean warnings, respect residential areas and use authorized access. Some popular trails or monuments require reservations. Do not enter closed routes or photograph cultural practices without consent, and keep reef-safe behavior central to any water activity.','Five to seven days for a varied island stay.','https://www.gohawaii.com/islands/oahu','Waikiki Diamond Head Oahu'),
 g('maui','Maui: Haleakala & Coastal Days','Maui’s summit, coastal stays and winding road excursions are different days. Choose a base and a small number of activities, and follow current local guidance about access and recovery-sensitive areas.','Begin with a nearby beach or cultural visit, then plan Haleakala as a separate high-elevation outing. Check the specific summit entry conditions. If driving a winding coastal route, limit stops and leave enough daylight for the return rather than chasing every waterfall.','Road access, park reservations and community guidance change. Summit temperatures differ sharply from the coast. Respect private land, no-parking signs and ocean warnings, and never assume a waterfall pool is safe to enter.','Five or more days on the island.','https://www.nps.gov/hale/planyourvisit/index.htm','Haleakala crater Maui'),
 g('hawaii-island','Hawaii Island: Volcanoes & Two Coasts','Hawaii Island has substantial road distances between Kona, Hilo and Hawaii Volcanoes National Park. Choose overnight bases by the landscapes you want to visit and avoid making every day a cross-island drive.','Use one coast for arrival and local visits, then transfer deliberately if the other side is important. Give the national park a dedicated day beginning with current visitor information. Choose only open trails and viewpoints and leave time for weather changes.','Volcanic activity, gases and closures can change quickly. Use NPS alerts and stay behind barriers; no guide can promise visible lava. High-elevation excursions require separate preparation, while ocean access should follow local conditions and advice.','A week with two carefully chosen bases.','https://www.nps.gov/havo/planyourvisit/index.htm','Hawaii Volcanoes National Park crater')])
];
export const usaGuides = usaHubs.flatMap(h=>h.guides);
export const usaRoutes = ['/usa/', ...usaHubs.flatMap(h=>[`/usa/${h.slug}/`,...h.guides.map(g=>g.url)])];
if(usaHubs.length!==24 || usaGuides.length!==72 || new Set(usaRoutes).size!==97) throw new Error('USA route manifest mismatch');
